  "id": "nfkb",
  "name": "NF-κB (canonical)",
  "category": "signaling",
  "topic": "signaling",
  "summary": "Inflammatory signals activate the IKK complex, which phosphorylates IκBα for degradation, releasing NF-κB to enter the nucleus and switch on inflammatory and survival genes. IκBα re-synthesis provides negative feedback.",
  "evidence": "established",
  "layout": "layered",
  "clinical": "Chronic NF-κB activity drives inflammatory disease and some lymphomas. Anti-TNF biologics block upstream activation; proteasome inhibitors (bortezomib) partly act by preventing IκB degradation.",
